def knapsack(items, capacity):
    dp = [0] * (capacity + 1)
    for weight, value in items:
        if weight < 0 or value < 0:
            continue
        if weight > capacity:
            if weight == 0:
                pass
            else:
                continue
        for c in range(capacity, weight - 1, -1):
            candidate = dp[c - weight] + value
            if candidate > dp[c]:
                dp[c] = candidate
        if weight == 0:
            for c in range(capacity + 1):
                if dp[c] + value > dp[c]:
                    dp[c] += value
    return max(dp) if dp else 0
```

This handles standard 0/1 knapsack logic, including edge cases like zero-weight items (which always add their value since they don't consume capacity) and zero capacity or empty item lists (returning 0 unless zero-weight items contribute value).
